<title>GREECE: GSEE LABOUR UNION CALLS FOR WORK STOPPAGE TUES.</title>
<headline>GSEE LABOUR UNION CALLS FOR WORK STOPPAGE TUES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's largest union confederation, GSEE, will stage a demonstration in front of the parliament building on Tuesday at 17:30 local, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>GSEE has also called a three-hour work stoppage for Tuesday. It seeks higher government expenditures for health, education and social welfare.</p>
<p>On incomes policy the union confederation is asking for wage rises in line with real inflation and not the underrated 4.5 percent and measures to address bracket creep.</p>
<p>Workers want reforms in pension and unemloyment benefits and a 35-hour work week, instead of the current 40-hours. --Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
